course: dictionary
lesson: 14880
title: Receptacle means a container
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A receptacle is a container, something that holds things. It is a formal word, so you will often see it on signs and in exams. «Please place litter in the receptacle provided.» The sign wants you to put rubbish in a bin, box or bowl that is there for it.
explain: Use the words around it to check the meaning. «Each receptacle holds three litres.» Litres measure how much liquid something can hold, so a receptacle must be something that holds things, like a jug or a tank. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Each container holds three litres» still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Some phrases show what kind of receptacle you mean. A waste receptacle is a bin for rubbish, and a litter receptacle is a bin for litter. «Put your apple core in the waste receptacle by the gate.» The phrase tells you where the apple core belongs.
fact: Receptacle is a formal noun meaning a container that holds things.
fact: A receptacle can be a bin, box or bowl.
fact: In the USA, a technical use of receptacle means an electrical socket on a wall, where a plug goes.
fact: In science, a receptacle is the part of a flower stalk that the flower grows from.
fact: Common phrases are waste receptacle and litter receptacle, both meaning a bin for rubbish.
exercise: «Please place litter in the receptacle provided.» What is a receptacle here? | A type of flower | A loud noise | *A container for litter
exercise: «Each receptacle holds three litres.» What does a receptacle do? | It runs very fast | *It holds things | It makes a loud noise | It grows in the ground
exercise: Which word is the formal word for a container that holds things? | Puddle | Gallop | Whisper | *Receptacle
test: Sam sees a waste receptacle by the gate. What is it for? | Playing football | Climbing up | *Rubbish | Sleeping
test: In the USA, what can a receptacle mean in a technical sense? | A type of cake | A kind of bird | *An electrical socket in the wall | A fast car
exam: Which word means a formal container for rubbish? | Pavement | Puddle | *Receptacle | Breeze
